course: dictionary
lesson: 7955
title: Receipts and proof
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A receipt is a piece of paper, or an email, from a shop. It shows what you bought, how much you paid and when. Shops give you receipts so you can prove you bought something.
explain: Use the words around a word to work out its meaning. «A receipt is proof of what you bought, when and for how much.» The word proof is a clue: a receipt is something that shows the truth about a purchase.
explain: «A gift receipt lets someone swap a present without seeing its price.» The clue is swap. A receipt lets you change something you were given, so you show the shop the paper and they exchange the item.
explain: The word has other uses too. On receipt of your letter means when you get your letter. In a business, receipts means the money it has taken in.
fact: A receipt is a piece of paper or an email from a shop.
fact: A receipt shows what you bought, how much you paid and when.
fact: «A receipt is proof of what you bought, when and for how much.»
fact: «Keep gift card codes and receipts safe until the card is used.»
fact: In the plural, receipts means the money a business has received.
exercise: «A receipt is proof of what you bought, when and for how much.» What is a receipt? | *A piece of paper or email from a shop that shows what you bought | A coin you find in the street | A letter from the bank | A bag for carrying shopping
exercise: «A gift receipt lets someone swap a present without seeing its price.» Why is a gift receipt useful? | It shows the present was wrapped | It makes the present cost more | *It lets someone swap a present without showing its price | It stops the shop from closing
exercise: Nadia says, «Keep the receipt.» What does she mean? | Tear it into small pieces | Give it to a friend | Put it in the bin | *Hold on to it safely
test: «On receipt of your letter, we will reply.» Here receipt means | A small piece of money | *The act of getting something | A shop that sells paper | A bill you pay later
test: Which thing shows how much you paid and when? | A map of the shop | A shopping list | *A till receipt | A birthday card
exam: Why should you keep a receipt? | *To prove what you bought, so you can return or exchange it | To use as a bookmark | To wrap a present in | To make the shop close early
